    {
      "type": "LinguisticObject",
      "content": "József Rippl-Rónai (died 1927), Paris and Kaposvár, Hungary; by descent to his widow, Lazarine Baudrion, from 1927 to at least 1934, when she consigned it to her husband’s estate auction [Budapest 1934]; sold to Mrs. Irén Balla (née Vida, died 1939), Pécs and Budapest, Hungary, by 1936 [Dénes 1936]; by descent to her husband, Dr. Adolf Balla [according to Rudolf Bedő’s unpublished memoir; copy in curatorial file]; sold to Rudolf Bedő (died 1978), Budapest, by at least January 1942 [according to an exhibition label on verso for Budapest 1942; copy in curatorial file.  See also the unpublished memoir cited above]; by descent to his wife, Mária Bedő (née Rott; died 1993), Budapest; by descent to their son, Gábor Bedő (died 2004), Budapest; by descent to his wife, Mrs. Gánéeé Bedő (née Erzsébet Magdolna Galambos) [according to Certificate of Transfer of Ownership, dated July 18, 2012; copy in curatorial file]; sold to Kieselbach Gallery, Budapest [according to certificate cited above]; sold to the Art Institute of Chicago, 2011.",
